 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 632223,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"6\">\n    <li>The company’s pricing plan states that the usage rate is constant for any number of minutes connected to the Internet. The number of minutes is related to the cost in dollars and has a linear relationship. The equation of the line is <span data-math=\"y = 0.03x +0.10\">y = 0.03x +0.10</span>. What does the slope represent in this situation?</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p><img alt=\"A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS NUMBER OF MINUTES ON THE X-AXIS AND TOTAL SESSION COST IN DOLLARS ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN THROUGH THE POINTS INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT.\" class=\"atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"318\" src=\"exercises/media/5b63af199437f382.jpg\" width=\"450\"></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1224144,
     "content_html": "For every 3 minutes of internet usage, the price increases 1 cent."
    },
    {
     "id": 1224145,
     "content_html": "For every minute of internet usage, the price increases 3 cents."
    }
   ],
